-- title:
--   Finite-adelic covolume identity with local correction factors
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K\subset L$ are number fields with $[L:K]=2$ (hypothesis `h2`) and $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (hypothesis `hgen`). Height-one primes of $\mathcal O_K$ are written $\mathfrak v$ below; for such $\mathfrak v$, $K_{\mathfrak v}$ denotes the adic completion and $q_{\mathfrak v}=\mathrm{absNorm}(\mathfrak v)$. For a $K$-algebra $A$, [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L202) is the entrywise action of $\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id}$ on $GL_2(L\otimes_K A)$, [`AutomorphicForm.normString`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L205) attaches to $\delta$ the product $\delta\cdot\sigma(\delta)$ of the first $[L:K]$ iterates, [`AutomorphicForm.toTensorGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L71) is the map $GL_2(A)\to GL_2(L\otimes_K A)$ induced by $a\mapsto 1\otimes a$, [`AutomorphicForm.twistedCentralizer`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L220) $K\,L\,A\,\sigma\,\delta$ is the subgroup $\{t\mid t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1}=\delta\}$, and [`AutomorphicForm.IsSigmaConjugate`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L208) $\delta\,\delta'$ means $\delta'=x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$ for some $x$, while [`AutomorphicForm.IsNormConjugator`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L214) $\gamma\,\delta\,y$ means $\mathrm{toTensorGL}(\gamma)=y^{-1}\,\mathrm{normString}(\delta)\,y$. All general linear groups and twisted centralisers carry their Borel $\sigma$-algebras.
--
--   The data are: an element $\delta_0\in GL_2(L)$, a unit $c$ of $L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K$ and a unit $u$ of $\mathbb A_K$. Write $\delta:=\iota(\delta_0)\cdot c\,I$ for the product of the image of $\delta_0$ under $L\to L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K$ with the scalar matrix $c$, and $\delta_{\mathfrak v}:=$ [`AutomorphicForm.tensorPlace`](def/AutomorphicForm_BaseChangePlaces.html#L49) $K\,L\,\mathfrak v\,\delta$, its image in $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v})$ under $\mathrm{id}_L\otimes(\text{evaluation at }\mathfrak v)$. Hypothesis `hN` states $\delta\cdot\sigma(\delta)=\mathrm{toTensorGL}(u\,I)$, and `hns` states that $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x)$ is never a scalar matrix $z\,I$ with $z\in L^\times$, for $x\in GL_2(L)$ and $z\in L^\times$.
--
--   Local measures: $\tau f'$ assigns to each $\mathfrak v$ a measure on the twisted centraliser of $\delta_{\mathfrak v}$, and `hτf'` requires each of these to be a Haar measure.
--
--   Normalisation data: a function $t$ from primes to $[0,\infty]$ and a finite set $S_0$ of primes with $t_{\mathfrak v}=1$ for $\mathfrak v\notin S_0$ (`ht`). The hypothesis `hfin` requires, for every $\mathfrak v$, one of two alternatives: either there exists $y\in GL_2(L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v})$ which is a norm conjugator taking the scalar matrix with entry $u_{\mathfrak v}$ (the image of $u\,I$ under `AdelicLevel.glFin` followed by `AdelicLevel.finComponent` at $\mathfrak v$) to $\mathrm{normString}(\delta_{\mathfrak v})$, and such that the pushforward of $\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}$ under $t\mapsto y^{-1}ty$ equals $t_{\mathfrak v}$ times the pushforward of [`AutomorphicForm.localHaar`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L168) $K\,\mathfrak v$ (the Haar measure on $GL_2(K_{\mathfrak v})$ normalised by the integral set) under $\mathrm{toTensorGL}$; or else no scalar matrix $z\,I$, $z\in(L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v})^\times$, is $\sigma$-conjugate to $\delta_{\mathfrak v}$ and, writing $E_{\mathfrak v}$ for the set of elements of the twisted centraliser whose determinant is the image of a unit $s\in K_{\mathfrak v}$ with $|s|=1$, the identity $\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}(E_{\mathfrak v})\cdot q_{\mathfrak v}=t_{\mathfrak v}+\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}(E_{\mathfrak v})$ holds. The hypothesis `hone` requires, for $\mathfrak v\notin S_0$, that $\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}$ give mass $1$ to the preimage in the twisted centraliser of [`AutomorphicForm.semiLocalIntegralSet`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L136) $K\,L\,\mathfrak v$, the set of $g$ with all entries of $g$ and of $g^{-1}$ in the image [`AutomorphicForm.semiLocalIntegers`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L98) of $\mathcal O_L\otimes_{\mathcal O_K}\mathcal O_{\mathfrak v}$ in $L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v}$.
--
--   Geometric data: a nonzero column $v\in L^2$, and an open compact subset $U$ of $(\mathbb A_{L,f})^2$ (`hUo`, `hUc`).
--
--   Level data: a finite set $S_1\supseteq S_0$ of primes (`hS₁`), and for each $\mathfrak v$ a Borel measurable set $W_{\mathfrak v}\subseteq GL_2(L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v})$ (`hWm`). The hypothesis `hW₀` requires, for $\mathfrak v\notin S_1$ and $x$ in the twisted centraliser of $\delta_{\mathfrak v}$, that $x\in W_{\mathfrak v}$ hold if and only if all entries of $x$ lie in the semilocal integers. The hypothesis `hW₁` requires, for every finite set $S\supseteq S_1$ and every $t$ in the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ over $\mathbb A_K$ all of whose local images at primes outside $S$ lie in the semilocal integral sets, the equality of complex numbers between the indicator of $U$ evaluated at the finite-adelic part of the vector obtained by applying the matrix over $\mathbb A_L$ attached to $t$ by the entrywise ring isomorphism $L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K\cong\mathbb A_K\otimes_K L\cong\mathbb A_L$ (`Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` followed by [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57)) to the column $(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,v_j)_j$, and the product over $\mathfrak v\in S$ of the indicators of $W_{\mathfrak v}$ at the local images of $t$. The hypothesis `hunit` requires, for $\mathfrak v\notin S_1$, the first alternative of `hfin` with scaling factor $1$: a norm conjugator $y$ as above for which the pushforward of $\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}$ under $t\mapsto y^{-1}ty$ equals the pushforward of the local Haar measure under $\mathrm{toTensorGL}$.
--
--   Correction factors: a function $\mathrm{Corr}$ of a prime and a real number with values in $[0,\infty]$. The hypothesis `hCorr` requires, for $\mathfrak v\in S_1$ and every real $s'\ge 1$,
--   $$\int_{\{t\,\in\,W_{\mathfrak v}\}}\bigl\|N_{(L\otimes_K K_{\mathfrak v})/K_{\mathfrak v}}\bigl(\det t\bigr)\bigr\|^{s'}\,d\tau f'_{\mathfrak v}=\mathrm{Corr}_{\mathfrak v}(s')\cdot\bigl(1-q_{\mathfrak v}^{-2s'}\bigr)^{-1}\bigl(1-q_{\mathfrak v}^{1-2s'}\bigr)^{-1},$$
--   the integral being a lower Lebesgue integral over the subset of the twisted centraliser whose underlying matrix group element lies in $W_{\mathfrak v}$. The hypothesis `hCorr₁` requires, for $\mathfrak v\in S_1$, that $\mathrm{Corr}_{\mathfrak v}(1)\ne\infty$ and that $\mathrm{Corr}_{\mathfrak v}$ tend to $\mathrm{Corr}_{\mathfrak v}(1)$ along the right-hand neighbourhood filter of $1$.
--
--   Basis data: a finite type $\iota$ with $\#\iota=4$ (`hι`) and a family $b:\iota\to M_2(L)$ which is $K$-linearly independent (`hb`) and whose $K$-span is exactly the twisted commutant, i.e. $Xb\delta_0=\delta_0\,\sigma(X)$ holds precisely when $X$ lies in the span of the range of $b$ (`hbspan`, stated as $X\delta_0=\delta_0\,X^{\sigma}$ if and only if $X\in\mathrm{span}_K(\mathrm{range}\,b)$).
--
--   Finally, $\mathbb A_K$ carries a measurable structure which is its Borel structure, and $\rho$ is an additive Haar measure on $\iota\to\mathbb A_K$.
--
--   Put
--   $$Q:=\mathrm{ofReal}\Bigl(\sqrt{\,|d_K|^{\#\iota}\cdot\bigl|N_{K/\mathbb Q}\det\bigl(\mathrm{Tr}_{L/K}\mathrm{tr}(b_ib_j)\bigr)_{i,j}\bigr|}\Bigr)\cdot\rho\{a\mid \forall k,\ a_k\in \mathrm{adelicBox}\,K\},$$
--   where $d_K$ is `NumberField.discr K` and [`NumberField.AdelicBox.adelicBox K`](def/NumberField_AdelicBox.html#L295) is the set of adeles whose archimedean component lies in `infiniteBox K` (the preimage of the fundamental domain of the lattice basis of $K$) and whose finite component is integral at every finite place.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions: first, $Q\ne 0$; second, $Q\ne\infty$; third,
--   $$\Bigl(\prod_{\mathfrak v\in S_1}\mathrm{Corr}_{\mathfrak v}(1)\Bigr)\cdot Q=\rho(\mathcal A)\cdot\Bigl(2^{\,2[K:\mathbb Q]}\cdot\prod_{\mathfrak v\in S_0}t_{\mathfrak v}\cdot\mathrm{ofReal}\bigl(d_K^2\bigr)\Bigr),$$
--   where $\mathcal A$ is the set of those $a:\iota\to\mathbb A_K$ such that each $a_k$ has archimedean component in `infiniteBox K` and such that the finite-adelic part of the vector $\Psi(a)\cdot(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,v_j)_j\in(\mathbb A_L)^2$ lies in $U$; here $\Psi(a)\in M_2(\mathbb A_L)$ is obtained from $\sum_k\,(b_k\text{ with each entry }l\mapsto l\otimes a_k)\in M_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K)$ by applying entrywise the ring isomorphism $L\otimes_K\mathbb A_K\cong\mathbb A_K\otimes_K L\cong\mathbb A_L$ used above.
--
--   This is the finite-adelic half of a covolume identity for the twisted commutant of $\delta_0$: the product of the local correction factors at $1$ over the bad set $S_1$, times the Gram-determinant covolume of the lattice spanned by $b$ against the adelic box, is computed as the $\rho$-volume of the set cut out by the archimedean box and the finite condition $\Psi(a)v\in U$, up to the explicit constant $2^{2[K:\mathbb Q]}\prod_{S_0}t_{\mathfrak v}\,d_K^2$. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.sqrt_det_gram_mul_lintegral_schwartzMap_archIdent_mul_prod_corr_eq_lintegral_pairHaar_mul_two_pow_mul_discr_sq_of_isOpen_isCompact`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.sqrt_det_gram_mul_lintegral_schwartzMap_archIdent_mul_prod_corr_eq_lintegral_pairHaar_mul_two_pow_mul_discr_sq_of_isOpen_isCompact), where it is combined with the corresponding archimedean computation.
